two decades on from the original launch  of the shahram volkswagen has given the  second generation a little makeover its  trademark quality such as the flexible  interior concept ride comfort and safety  are still on board  plus a couple of new goodies that's  official Sharan has sold around 800,000  units since 1995 explains our car  reviewer Klaus it's a real family car  and was in fact originally twinned with  a Sayeda humba and the Ford Galaxie this  latest version of the second generation  is very similar to the outgoing model  there are minimal changes on the outside  but more significant ones under the hood  and in the cabin the design of the  seven-seater MPV is more or less the  same among the new editions bolder front  lamps and LED lights at the rear  as always the sliding doors mean easy  access for passengers  the interior boasts classic VW hallmarks  the layout absolutely driver friendly  the Chiron boasts a wide range of  storage options literally all over the  cabin the variable seating concept has  likewise been retained the standard  cargo volume is 822 litres with the  seats down rising to almost 2300 liters  the Chiron is no lightweight points out  Klaus it weighs in at one point seven  tons so if you then load it fully you  might find it tilts a little around  bends but it's always safe the 2-liter  TDI version we tested generates 85  kilowatts and has a top speed of 184  km/h the NPV can make the dash to 100  km/h and twelve point six seconds  official fuel consumption is 5.1 liters  per 100 kilometers with co2 emissions of  132 grams per kilometer the magic word  these days has Klaus is connectivity and  this Chiron meets the requirements you  can plug in your smart phone to this  multimedia system allowing you to view  your phone display on the monitor  while your phone is connected to the  system you can call up the most  important functions on the color TFT  display you can browse through your  archive of music tracks for example and  pick one to play via the touchscreen the  Sharan also scores on the driver assist  front with an array of features safety  is a big priority with the vehicles  makers explains Klaus which is why it  has a collection of electronic assist  unmatched in its class  there's the multi-collision brake or the  rear traffic alert system where the  monitor warns the driver of passing  vehicles while exiting a parking space  open each team on sofa difficult for the  first time the Saran has been fitted  with adaptive cruise control a further  boost to safety when driving down  highways or on longer journeys  the guns Klaus has saved the really  positive aspect until last the new  edition costs no more than its  predecessor 32,000 euros for the base  model which comes with a gasoline engine  that diesel equivalent costs just under  thirty three and a half thousand they  say never change a winning team and  that's certainly true with the VW Sharan
 

